<title>INDIA: India produced 3,095 tonnes copper cathodes in May.</title>
<headline>India produced 3,095 tonnes copper cathodes in May.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Hindustan Copper Ltd (HCL) produced 3,095 tonnes of copper cathodes in May against a target of 3,750 tonnes, a government statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>HCL also produced 3,225 tonnes of continous cast copper rods</p>
<p>in May against a target 3,500 tonnes, the statement said.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	    Installed     May, 1997	Cumulative output</p>
<p>	    capacity	---------	-----------------</p>
<p>	    (annual)	 Actual	 Apr-May 97  Apr-May 96</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> cathodes   47,500	 3,095	    6,857	 6,446</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> rods	 60,000	 3,225	    5,525	 6,284</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
